{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause independently confirmed; fix pushed as Gerrit 3031 (`94164649f8f`)\n\nThe prior ghost-attribute theory was re-investigated from scratch rather than accepted,\nand it holds. The decisive evidence is arithmetic, not inference:\n\n```\nsha1(base64decode(\"ca14e455f4ba60b0c742bc92e864360fbed3217b\"))\n  == \"83b0f4d19f5b4f86107c592278234e5f30958a79\"\n```\n\nThat is exactly the before/after pair in the live plan. The provider is iterating the\n`user_data` hash on its own previous output, which is why the attribute can never\nconverge and why two consecutive plans agree while any two plans separated by an apply\ndo not.\n\n### The payload was never the problem\n\n`user_data_base64` is byte-identical across all three places it exists — Terraform state,\nlive EC2 `UserData.Value`, and a freshly computed `base64gzip(templatefile(...))`:\n\n```\nb64_sha256     48dbd61e9bfd38ee3179ea55dbf5366d4c8d750cd4ee46aa662f2f3f5b072bbd\ngzip_sha1      dfbff29a173b119945ea3585bd422180f909d78b\ninflated_sha1  2b606702978bfecaa16233adaa95aeefab160926\n```\n\nProvider source for the pinned `hashicorp/aws v5.100.0` confirms the asymmetry that\ncreates the ghost: `user_data` carries `StateFunc: userDataHashSum`, `user_data_base64`\ndoes not, and refresh sets only `user_data_base64` when that key is present — so a\n`user_data` value left in state by the earlier plain-`user_data` representation is never\ncleared. The nearby comments in `main.tf` about abandoning plain `user_data` at the\n16,384-byte limit are how it got there.\n\n### The fix is one element, not a new policy\n\n`aws_instance.gerrit` already carried `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [ami] }`. The change\nadds `user_data` to that existing list and nothing else:\n\n```hcl\nignore_changes = [ami, user_data]\n```\n\nThis is not masking a payload problem, because there is no payload problem. It stops\nTerraform planning against a state-only attribute that the configuration does not set and\nthat AWS does not have. `user_data_base64` stays fully managed.\n\n### AC3 — regression check\n\n`tests/unit/test_terraform_gerrit_user_data_churn.py` fails if `user_data` is dropped from\n`ignore_changes`, and also fails if `user_data_base64` is ever added to it — because\nignoring the real payload would silently stop managing the instance's boot configuration,\nwhich is a worse regression than the one being fixed.\n\nRed/green: before the fix, `assert 'user_data' in {'ami'}` (1 failed, 1 passed); after,\n2 passed.\n\n### AC4 — no replacement, confirmed from plan JSON\n\nPost-fix saved plan reports `aws_instance.gerrit` as `actions: [\"no-op\"]`,\n`replace_paths: null`, `replacement_count: 0`, `user_data_base64_equal: true`. The Gerrit\nresource leaves the diff entirely: `Plan: 8 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy`. The 8\nremaining adds are the `lmn_private_context_denied` alarms, which are not this ticket's.\n\n### Scope note\n\nThe commit also hardens `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py`, which `make verify` exposed as\nhost-load-sensitive: it asserted a tight `<2.0s` wall-clock threshold. It now asserts\nactual coroutine cancellation. Disclosed here because it is outside this ticket's declared\nfile impact; it was fixed rather than retried, per the flaky-test rule.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` passes. Complexity ratchet `active=32 new=0 increased=0 stale=17`; mechanism\nratchet `active=682 new=26 increased=0 stale=0`, admitted entries only. `make verify` shows\nexactly the 17 known macOS-arm64 pandoc failures.\n\n### AC2 — not claimed\n\nNo production apply was run. `scripts/terraform_prod.py` correctly refuses a fix branch\nthat is not the fetched `origin/main` tip, so the mediated apply can only happen after\n3031 merges."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789978430325655404,"uuid":"8a21a371-0a13-4860-90d0-c72e523993c6"}